### Build

```bash
$ make build
```

### Run

```bash
$ ./build/{{ project_slug }} --help
$ ./build/{{ project_slug }} --version
```

`--version` prints the version the Makefile compiles in: the one CI is releasing, or `git describe --tags` for a local build, or `0.0.0` with no tags or no git.

### Conditional Compilation

| Flag              | Set by         | Effect                                                         |
|-------------------|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `PROJECT_NAME`    | Makefile       | Program name shown by `--help` and `--version`                 |
| `PROJECT_VERSION` | Makefile       | Version the Makefile works out; see Run above                  |
| `NODEBUG`         | `make release` | Drops `debug()` output and the file, line and errno from logs  |



## Testing

### Run all tests

```bash
$ make test
```

Runs cppcheck over `src/`, then checks the built binary's `--help` and `--version` with `tests/cli.sh`.

### Formatting

```bash
$ make format           # format in place
$ make format-dry-run   # list files that need formatting
```

The layout follows the [NASA SEL C Style Guide](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19950022400) (SEL-94-003), set out in `.clang-format`. `src/debug.h` keeps its own layout and is not formatted.



