## Release

`make release` builds the project for each release target chosen when it was generated{% if release_targets | reject('equalto', 'none') | list %} ({{ release_targets | join(', ') }}){% endif %}, writing one binary per target into `dist/`. With no targets, `dist/` is left empty.

The targets are set in the `Makefile`, in `RELEASE_TARGETS`, and cross-compiled with zig by `scripts/release.sh`. Linux builds link musl statically.



## Copier Update

The project uses [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) to manage its template. When the template is updated, the project can be easily brought up to date by running the following command from the project root:

```bash
$ copier update --defaults --answers-file .copier-cxx-answers.yml
```
When the `--defaults` option is used, copier update skips all previously answered questions and prompts only for newly introduced ones.

